# Sports League Management System — JSON / localStorage Version

A client-side, single-page CRUD application for managing a much larger sports-league data model (20 entity modules), built with React + TypeScript, persisting entirely to the browser's `localStorage` — no backend or real database. Built as a semester project for **CS-304 Database Systems**.

**Team:**
- Yasir Hameed (24-CyS-002)
- Muhammad Anish (24-CyS-014)
- Muhammad Taha (24-CyS-068)

## Features

- Full CRUD (Create / Read / Update / Delete) across **20 modules**: Coaches, Teams, Players, Venues, Seasons, Schedules, Matches, Scores, Game Logs, Standings, Statistics, Player Profiles, Injuries, Awards, Equipment, Sponsors, Posters, Tickets, Fan Registration, and References (audit log)
- Dashboard with total record count and module count across the whole dataset
- Foreign-key–style relationships resolved at render time (e.g. a match's team/venue/season IDs are displayed as names, not raw IDs), with dropdown selects populated from related tables
- Per-field validation: required fields, min/max length, numeric ranges, email format, letters-only names, duplicate checks
- Global search across the currently open module (matches raw values and resolved foreign-key values)
- Toast notifications for create/update/delete feedback
- Data persists across page reloads via `localStorage` (key: `sports_league_db_v2`); a reset action is available to restore seed data

## Tech stack

- **React** 19 + **TypeScript**
- **Vite** (build tool, with `vite-plugin-singlefile` for single-file builds)
- **Tailwind CSS** 4
- `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` for conditional class handling
- No backend — all data lives in `localStorage` as JSON

## Setup / Run

```bash
npm install
npm run dev        # start local dev server
npm run build       # production build
npm run preview     # preview the production build
```

Requires Node.js (any recent LTS version). No database or server setup needed — just open the app in a browser.

## Files

```
json-localstorage-version/
├── index.html
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
├── vite.config.ts
├── docs/
│   ├── Peoject Proposal__DBs(A).pdf     # Initial project proposal
│   └── DBS Project Report.pdf           # Final report
└── src/
    ├── main.tsx           # App entry point
    ├── App.tsx            # Main app shell — routing, search, modal state
    ├── components.tsx     # Reusable CRUDTable, FormModal, ToastContainer
    ├── schema.tsx          # Definitions for all 20 modules (fields, columns, FK lookups)
    ├── store.ts            # localStorage persistence layer + validation logic
    ├── index.css           # Global styles (Tailwind entry)
    └── utils/cn.ts         # Classname merge helper
```

## Note

`node_modules/` and `package-lock.json` build artifacts are excluded via `.gitignore` — after cloning, run `npm install` to regenerate dependencies.
